    "bodyDocument": {
      "textSnapshot": "Problem:\nThe entire doctor command would crash with \"could not open TTY\" errors when run in non-interactive environments (agents, CI) because it tried to open TTY prompts without checking if an interactive terminal was available. Stuck sessions and disconnected metadata checks would fail instead of providing useful diagnostics.\nSolution:\nAdded guards to check interactive.CanPromptInteractively() before opening any TTY prompts in the doctor command. When running non-interactively, the command now:\nDisplays each stuck session's diagnosis (no early exit after the first one)\nShows what action --force would take on each session (condense or discard)\nHints users to run entire doctor --force to apply fixes\nLeaves sessions untouched for later interactive processing\nDegrades gracefully for disconnected metadata checks with the same hint\nUpdated help text to document the non-interactive behavior and added tests to verify sessions are diagnosed without crashes and remain intact for manual action."
    }
  }
}
"}

